{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss","id":1513657,"title":"COFD Fan Gameline where you play as a final boss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-02T09:01:47-07:00","id":1513657,"title":"COFD Fan Gameline where you play as a final boss","content":"After a great deal of thinking, I started on a fan gameline that I'll need a massive amount of help with. I might even make a discord server for it. It's called Dark Master: The (haven't figured this out yet).<br /> <br /> I'll link to the google drive with it, but I'll explain some of the things I was thinking about when designing it.<br /> <br /> The game is a study of evil and innately evil creatures, what it is like to be one of them and how hard it is for them to be good. Good and evil are often subjective (which is probably part of the reason why Morality was changed to Integrity), so to get around that, I made it so that the main sense of good and evil that matters for a Dark Master is the sense of morality of the god who created them. So, the player, the GM, and the Dark Master could potentially think of something as good but the god who created the Dark Master could think of it as evil. But most gods will think the same basic things are evil that humans think of as evil, like murder being evil. There are some rewards for being good, but they are few and far between.<br /> <br /> Next, Dark Masters are innately evil but they aren't entirely evil. For example, they show genuine sympathy to Demons, Changelings, and Deviants due to their similar situations. They also are disgusted with anyone who is evil and is tricking themselves into thinking they're the good guys, and they believe this applies to the Beasts. The Dark Masters know exactly what they are. They also hate all gods, which means they hate Leviathans.<br /> <br /> Dark Masters are also incredibly arrogant, so you'll see lines from them where they're doing stupid things that'll get them killed. For example, saying &quot;I want to kill Luna&quot; to a group of werewolves.<br /> <br /> In terms of game mechanics, most of them have the whole innately evil thing in mind. I made it very easy for Dark Masters to be evil. Being evil makes them more powerful, doing evil actions might get them more of the supernatural energy stat, and becoming too good will harm them. I tried to make the game mechanics support the Dark Master mindset as well. For example, their virtue equivalent is called megalomania.<br /> <br /> Now, for combat, Dark Masters should be like bosses in video games. They shouldn't be afraid of fighting but they should be cautious of it. They should be the sort who make their enemies fight waves of minions or make their way through a trap-filled dungeon before fighting them. In combat itself, the Dark Masters should be powerful but far from unbeatable.<br /> <br /> To facilitate this, I made the Dark Masters the second most immortal creatures out there. Only Geists are more immortal. However, I put in consequences for their death, namely in how long it takes them to come back. Essentially, a Dark Master comes back from dying but can permanently die under circumstances that are stated in the doc. And even if they aren't permanently killed, they could be set massively back from a defeat. I'm just not sure about the minion numbers and their general power in combat. I'm not sure if they're powerful enough, too powerful, or not powerful enough.<br /> <br /> And that's a good chunk of my line of thinking when I made this. Here's the doc:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zTQQpRQHiNBvdPXGpK4AbRsmH6Fy_IvJy7pKKWY6Mt0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zTQQpRQHiNBvdPXGpK4AbRsmH6Fy_IvJy7pKKWY6Mt0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zTQQpRQHiNBvdPXGpK4AbRsmH6Fy_IvJy7pKKWY6Mt0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zTQQpRQHiNBvdPXGpK4AbRsmH6Fy_IvJy7pKKWY6Mt0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T09:56:48-07:00","id":1513663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss#post1513657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To facilitate this, I made the Dark Masters the second most immortal creatures out there. Only Geists are more immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So my general response to this has been &quot;THat's pretty much every monster ever out there&quot; with some particular emphasis on mages(Wizarding arrogance being usefully applied accross the board doing a lot to win followers and develop a cult that purusues your amoral Obsessions and Beasts(all of htat, but baked in amorality is kind of the default starting line), but the one that stood out the most to me is mummies, and this line really cemented &quot;You mean you want The Arisen&quot; was this one.<br /> <br /> Because my fellow in this wild world, The Arisen are the most immortal thing out there, were built around the idea of &quot;Fuck it, you play the Prince&quot;, can be devastating in combat but need to be precise in their application, and are basically agents of a brutal pre-agricultural mindset and literal god entities that are shadows of a literal Law of Suffering.<br /> <br /> But, like, seriously, the Arisen are hella fucking immortal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:51:46-07:00","id":1513688,"title":"","content":"From a basic play issue perspective, there's a major problem with any game where the PCs aren't really capable of forming a group so that everyone playing can play together over an extended period of time. Nobody wants to spend all the effort to find a RPG group, start a game, and then have it dissolve into backstabbing until one player and the ST run a solo game while the rest either leave or have to sit and watch without anything to do.<br /> <br /> In general, this suffers the biggest issue fan-splat suffer: the concept is too narrow. There are lots of existing CofD games that have ways to execute the &quot;evil overlord&quot; concept, without it being the only viable concept of the game. Having the only real &quot;splat&quot; be philosophic means any functional group of PCs need to have compatible philosophies since there's nothing else to connect them together. A fan-splat that's actually made for people that to solo play isn't an inherently bad thing, but if you're going to do that you need to lean into it with more than just pronouncements about how the character type doesn't get along with people enough to form a group.<br /> <br /> The very prescriptive relationships of Dark Masters and the rest of the inhabitants of the setting is also very off-putting and rather out of step with the CofD's preference to let such matters vary by time and location as individual personalities matter the most.<br /> <br /> I can't think of a single character this supports, that I can't make in one of the existing CofD games, which would be more fun to do because then I could play with other people too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:17:27-07:00","id":1513696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513663#post1513663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my general response to this has been &quot;THat's pretty much every monster ever out there&quot; with some particular emphasis on mages(Wizarding arrogance being usefully applied accross the board doing a lot to win followers and develop a cult that purusues your amoral Obsessions and Beasts(all of htat, but baked in amorality is kind of the default starting line), but the one that stood out the most to me is mummies, and this line really cemented &quot;You mean you want The Arisen&quot; was this one.<br /> <br /> Because my fellow in this wild world, The Arisen are the most immortal thing out there, were built around the idea of &quot;Fuck it, you play the Prince&quot;, can be devastating in combat but need to be precise in their application, and are basically agents of a brutal pre-agricultural mindset and literal god entities that are shadows of a literal Law of Suffering.<br /> <br /> But, like, seriously, the Arisen are hella fucking immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. I never really thought of the Arisen as immortal because they tend to not keep their memories every time they come back to life. I think of them the same way I think of characters who reincarnate, but you're right that they are incredibly immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T13:26:41-07:00","id":1513699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513688#post1513688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a basic play issue perspective, there's a major problem with any game where the PCs aren't really capable of forming a group so that everyone playing can play together over an extended period of time. Nobody wants to spend all the effort to find a RPG group, start a game, and then have it dissolve into backstabbing until one player and the ST run a solo game while the rest either leave or have to sit and watch without anything to do.<br /> <br /> In general, this suffers the biggest issue fan-splat suffer: the concept is too narrow. There are lots of existing CofD games that have ways to execute the &quot;evil overlord&quot; concept, without it being the only viable concept of the game. Having the only real &quot;splat&quot; be philosophic means any functional group of PCs need to have compatible philosophies since there's nothing else to connect them together. A fan-splat that's actually made for people that to solo play isn't an inherently bad thing, but if you're going to do that you need to lean into it with more than just pronouncements about how the character type doesn't get along with people enough to form a group.<br /> <br /> The very prescriptive relationships of Dark Masters and the rest of the inhabitants of the setting is also very off-putting and rather out of step with the CofD's preference to let such matters vary by time and location as individual personalities matter the most.<br /> <br /> I can't think of a single character this supports, that I can't make in one of the existing CofD games, which would be more fun to do because then I could play with other people too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've misunderstood things a bit. Dark Masters can work together without stabbing each other in the back, I even wrote that there are groups of Dark Masters who can work together in the google drive. It's just rare and difficult for them to work together. The players are meant to be the exceptions, the Dark Masters who can work together perfectly fine. That itself gives them an edge over other Dark Masters. Should I make it more clear that it's possible, but just rare, for Dark Masters to work together without betraying each other?<br /> <br /> As for the only philosophic thing, the impression I've got from other splats is that it should be perfectly fine for PCs to only be part of the same group. Like, I don't expect an Invictus Vampire to hang out with a Carthian to give an extreme example. Still, I didn't think that giving them other splats was a good idea since Dark Masters are supposed to be individually crafted. This was in part to give the players the most freedom because a mistake I made in a previous splat I was thinking of gave players very little freedom.<br /> <br /> But you're right that it's very narrow. There are many different possible types of evil overlords in fiction, so there is a lot of wiggle room within that, but you're still right that it's fairly narrow. As for the relationships, that's another good point. Dark Masters are highly variable, so they really shouldn't have a stereotypes section as they are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T15:39:48-07:00","id":1513716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513699#post1513699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've misunderstood things a bit. Dark Masters can work together without stabbing each other in the back, I even wrote that there are groups of Dark Masters who can work together in the google drive. It's just rare and difficult for them to work together. The players are meant to be the exceptions, the Dark Masters who can work together perfectly fine. That itself gives them an edge over other Dark Masters. Should I make it more clear that it's possible, but just rare, for Dark Masters to work together without betraying each other?<br /> <br /> As for the only philosophic thing, the impression I've got from other splats is that it should be perfectly fine for PCs to only be part of the same group. Like, I don't expect an Invictus Vampire to hang out with a Carthian to give an extreme example. Still, I didn't think that giving them other splats was a good idea since Dark Masters are supposed to be individually crafted. This was in part to give the players the most freedom because a mistake I made in a previous splat I was thinking of gave players very little freedom.<br /> <br /> But you're right that it's very narrow. There are many different possible types of evil overlords in fiction, so there is a lot of wiggle room within that, but you're still right that it's fairly narrow. As for the relationships, that's another good point. Dark Masters are highly variable, so they really shouldn't have a stereotypes section as they are now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize the broader idea you're going for (and can immediately counter argue it with Beast and Contagion Chronicles), but I do have to highlight how accidentally bad the Invictus working with the Carthians is in a Second Edition context. The Carthians inherently have a lot of advantages that make them advantageous for taking care of Elysium's rules and regulations, and the Invictus offer a point of stability that the Carthians can fall back on to when social experiments begin to run out of control-and in Second Edition, there's just as much predilection to take advantage of that as to make a point of opposition. Requiem Second Edition makes it really clear that the opposition that often forms the heart of Elysium politics is no longer so linear and fixed as it was in First Edition, and strange alliances can emerge depending on the setting.<br /> <br /> I'll come back later for the larger issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T16:19:57-07:00","id":1513722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513699#post1513699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you've misunderstood things a bit. Dark Masters can work together without stabbing each other in the back, I even wrote that there are groups of Dark Masters who can work together in the google drive. It's just rare and difficult for them to work together. The players are meant to be the exceptions, the Dark Masters who can work together perfectly fine. That itself gives them an edge over other Dark Masters. Should I make it more clear that it's possible, but just rare, for Dark Masters to work together without betraying each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can't really manage a compromise here. Either you need to establish a natural path for cooperation between Dark Masters (even Beast and Mummy manage it), or lean into it being meant to be a more solo oriented game; there's a lot of people out there that want solo oriented games because it's so hard to get games together with multiple people these days.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean making them &quot;nice.&quot; Vampires are notably cutthroat, but coteries (even diverse ones with members from multiple Covenants) have strong reasons to exist; especially for younger characters that need allies they can at least trust to have self-interest in mind. There's countless examples of villain team-ups to draw on because even evil can see the strength in numbers. The Dark Masters also have a clear mutual drive in antagonism towards their creators. I think if you want to increase the feeling of Dark Masters grouping up more natural than the text (when I read it earlier I haven't gotten back to it if you've done some edits), there needs to be things that drive them together. That can be something antagonistic like the Strix or Gentry, but it can also be something more &quot;natural&quot; to the splat like Mysteries for mages or how the Apex motivates collective actions by Beasts. Strength in numbers, even for good characters, only really makes sense to worry about if individual strength isn't enough to handle what's going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the only philosophic thing, the impression I've got from other splats is that it should be perfectly fine for PCs to only be part of the same group. Like, I don't expect an Invictus Vampire to hang out with a Carthian to give an extreme example. Still, I didn't think that giving them other splats was a good idea since Dark Masters are supposed to be individually crafted. This was in part to give the players the most freedom because a mistake I made in a previous splat I was thinking of gave players very little freedom. </div> </div> </div>There isn't a problem with just having a philosophic splat. The bigger issue is making sure that they can cooperate. In most games you can have everyone be members of the same Y-splat, because you have the X-splats to add variety too. If you're just going to have one splat, and groups for the PCs to form, the philosophies need to have common points so mixed groups make sense as well as unified groups. Beast, Changeling, and Deviant all offer a lot of customization as each of them are relatively &quot;unique&quot; as they were shaped by outside forces, but the playable philosophies are ones that can vary in groups successfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T06:45:59-07:00","id":1513764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513716#post1513716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realize the broader idea you're going for (and can immediately counter argue it with Beast and Contagion Chronicles), but I do have to highlight how accidentally bad the Invictus working with the Carthians is in a Second Edition context. The Carthians inherently have a lot of advantages that make them advantageous for taking care of Elysium's rules and regulations, and the Invictus offer a point of stability that the Carthians can fall back on to when social experiments begin to run out of control-and in Second Edition, there's just as much predilection to take advantage of that as to make a point of opposition. Requiem Second Edition makes it really clear that the opposition that often forms the heart of Elysium politics is no longer so linear and fixed as it was in First Edition, and strange alliances can emerge depending on the setting.<br /> <br /> I'll come back later for the larger issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood and thanks. I honestly think that my understanding of MTA and VTR has increased. There seem to be quite a few things I missed in those books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T06:48:15-07:00","id":1513765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513722#post1513722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you can't really manage a compromise here. Either you need to establish a natural path for cooperation between Dark Masters (even Beast and Mummy manage it), or lean into it being meant to be a more solo oriented game; there's a lot of people out there that want solo oriented games because it's so hard to get games together with multiple people these days.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean making them &quot;nice.&quot; Vampires are notably cutthroat, but coteries (even diverse ones with members from multiple Covenants) have strong reasons to exist; especially for younger characters that need allies they can at least trust to have self-interest in mind. There's countless examples of villain team-ups to draw on because even evil can see the strength in numbers. The Dark Masters also have a clear mutual drive in antagonism towards their creators. I think if you want to increase the feeling of Dark Masters grouping up more natural than the text (when I read it earlier I haven't gotten back to it if you've done some edits), there needs to be things that drive them together. That can be something antagonistic like the Strix or Gentry, but it can also be something more &quot;natural&quot; to the splat like Mysteries for mages or how the Apex motivates collective actions by Beasts. Strength in numbers, even for good characters, only really makes sense to worry about if individual strength isn't enough to handle what's going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There isn't a problem with just having a philosophic splat. The bigger issue is making sure that they can cooperate. In most games you can have everyone be members of the same Y-splat, because you have the X-splats to add variety too. If you're just going to have one splat, and groups for the PCs to form, the philosophies need to have common points so mixed groups make sense as well as unified groups. Beast, Changeling, and Deviant all offer a lot of customization as each of them are relatively &quot;unique&quot; as they were shaped by outside forces, but the playable philosophies are ones that can vary in groups successfully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I think I'm going to go for the group feature.<br /> <br /> Now, I really like your idea of playing up the animosity between them and the gods. Maybe the Dark Masters all know that the gods are coming for them sooner or later? Despite their egos, the Dark Masters know full well that they aren't a match for the gods alone. So, maybe they form groups with each other primarily to deal with the threat of the gods, as well as the other benefits to being in groups?<br /> <br /> And perhaps I could include a mechanic where Dark Masters can link or combine their dungeons? That could help incentivize their teamwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T10:13:20-07:00","id":1513790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513765#post1513765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I think I'm going to go for the group feature.<br /> <br /> Now, I really like your idea of playing up the animosity between them and the gods. Maybe the Dark Masters all know that the gods are coming for them sooner or later? Despite their egos, the Dark Masters know full well that they aren't a match for the gods alone. So, maybe they form groups with each other primarily to deal with the threat of the gods, as well as the other benefits to being in groups?<br /> <br /> And perhaps I could include a mechanic where Dark Masters can link or combine their dungeons? That could help incentivize their teamwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read Beast: the Primoridal? Cause that's going to resolve a lot of your questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T14:08:44-07:00","id":1513811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513790#post1513790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read Beast: the Primoridal? Cause that's going to resolve a lot of your questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have read it before, and I know about their lair mechanic, but it was a long time ago and I didn't like Beast, so I haven't read it since. I might read it again just for the lair mechanics, though. They aren't dungeons, due to the lack of minions, but I might be able to figured out something based on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T14:25:32-07:00","id":1513815,"title":"","content":"The Beast Player's Guide added a lot of Lair expanding stuff, including the ability to create minions to occupy your Lair. Having a ton of them isn't that easy (though keep in mind that &quot;lots of things that are only dangerous because of their vast numbers,&quot; can be a description of some of the environmental damage dealing Lair traits rather than stated out beings to contend with), but it does mean you can add some &quot;minibosses&quot; for Heroes/etc. to have to contend with as they explore your Lair before they run int you. There's also some Lair Merits that make it much easier for non-Beast allies to help you defend your Lair (such as making your Lair have amenities like &quot;real&quot; food and water so you can have living allies in there for long periods of time, and an Internet connection to both talk to them while you're outside your Lair and so they don't get bored).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T23:26:56-07:00","id":1513843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513811#post1513811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have read it before, and I know about their lair mechanic, but it was a long time ago and I didn't like Beast, so I haven't read it since. I might read it again just for the lair mechanics, though. They aren't dungeons, due to the lack of minions, but I might be able to figured out something based on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I primarily brought it up as a subject to plunder, and as Heavy Arms brought up, there are lair traits that facilitates Minions (the Minion and Thrall Lair Traits specifically from the BPG) as well as Horrorspawn, Primordial Cults, the benefits of Kinship, etc.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I finally checked out the document, and I am going to have to ask what it was that you didn't like about Beast, because...It kind of seems like you mostly want a reskinned Beast with increased &quot;hard to kill&quot; factor with your project, not gonna lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T04:54:15-07:00","id":1513859,"title":"","content":"And you could make a pretty simple change in Beast from &quot;destroying a Lair's Heart is an insta-kill on the Beast,&quot; to, &quot;if you don't destroy the Heart the Beast will come back eventually,&quot; and you'd get a lot of the &quot;hard to truly kill&quot; factor as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T06:32:40-07:00","id":1513869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513843#post1513843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I primarily brought it up as a subject to plunder, and as Heavy Arms brought up, there are lair traits that facilitates Minions (the Minion and Thrall Lair Traits specifically from the BPG) as well as Horrorspawn, Primordial Cults, the benefits of Kinship, etc.<br /> <br /> I will admit that I finally checked out the document, and I am going to have to ask what it was that you didn't like about Beast, because...It kind of seems like you mostly want a reskinned Beast with increased &quot;hard to kill&quot; factor with your project, not gonna lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things that I don't like about Beast, and I will admit that the Dark Master thing is somewhat similar to Beast, but many of my inspirations didn't have much to do with Beast. So, I'll tell you what I don't like about Beast that I'm avoiding here. Because while Dark Masters are similar to Beasts, there are some key differences.<br /> 1. There is no kinship. Dark Masters don't have an innate connection to the other creatures in the Chronicles of Darkness world that makes them more likely to like them.<br /> 2. Beasts seem to be under the impression that they're the good guys, or at least that their actions are excusable because they teach lessons. The Dark Masters know full well that they're evil and most of what they do is exclusively for their own benefit. Though, it is possible for a Dark Master to be good, just incredibly difficult.<br /> 3. The transformation mechanics I'm using are based on the mechanics from Demon but simplified because I like the Demon mechanics more than the Beast ones.<br /> <br /> There are a number of other reasons why I don't like Beast, but they aren't relevant to Dark Masters.<br /> <br /> And now, other differences that aren't connected to things I don't like in Beast (as in, they either aren't connected to Beast at all or they are connected to things that I'm oaky with in Beast):<br /> 1. I don't mind that the Lairs in Beast aren't in the physical world, but the Dark Master dungeons are in the physical world. This is, in essence, to put them in more constant danger. They have to worry about far more threats attacking them than the Beasts do.<br /> 2. Minions are a big part of Dark Master while they aren't in Beast. It's why there are core mechanics tied into Dark Power for their creation and not just merits. I'm also giving the players the hunter the vigil monster creation rules for their minions so they can be incredibly customizable.<br /> 3. Dark Masters do not create heroes or harm people with their mere existence. Instead, they have a very strong urge and incentive to act evil with it even making them more powerful.<br /> 4. The increased durability thing is meant to serve the idea behind how combat works in this game. Dark Masters should not be afraid of combat, but they should be cautious about it. There are still potential consequences for them dying, so they should be the sort to send their minions in first to weaken the enemy before coming in themselves. This is both inside and outside the lair. The increased hard to kill factor was something that I debated with myself a lot before going with it.<br /> 5. The gods are the enemies of the Dark Masters, and I'll probably rewrite it so that the Dark Masters are gathering in groups because they know the gods are coming for them. As for the Beasts, the True Fae respect and fear them and their goddess is fully on their side.<br /> 6. Dark Masters have grand ambitions as a core part of their gameplay. I've seen gamelines (I think a fan gameline, Genius the Transgression, but I don't remember for sure) where a fourth aspiration is added in. What I did was change that Aspiration into their Virtue equivelant (their Megalomania) because it's something that can never be truly satisfied. Basically, Dark Masters persue their own personal goals and such.<br /> 7. The Dark Masters aren't easily set into types. For player versatility and based on feedback I got for a previous fan gameline attempt, I didn't include an X-Splat, just a Y-Splat. Each Dark Master is hand-crafted by a god and can be fairly unique.<br /> 8. I included a rule that gives Dark Masters the option to make their transformation at the cost of weakening the transformation. This also has the cost that it gives the Dark Master a greater need to hide than most other Dark Masters and most (though not all) other player splats in Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> 9. The Dark Masters are fundamentally meant to be final bosses or commanders of dungeons. They are anything from Sephiroth to Sauron to Ainz to the Overlord from the Overlord games to the Dungeon Keeper. They are not meant to be the monsters of myth or nightmares.<br /> <br /> Thank you for this feedback and I hope this helps. If the Dark Masters come off as reskinned Beasts, then it means that I have some massive failings and really need the help. The fundamental premise is supposed to be different than in Beast, and I tried to make the mechanics with the premise in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T06:37:02-07:00","id":1513870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513815#post1513815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast Player's Guide added a lot of Lair expanding stuff, including the ability to create minions to occupy your Lair. Having a ton of them isn't that easy (though keep in mind that &quot;lots of things that are only dangerous because of their vast numbers,&quot; can be a description of some of the environmental damage dealing Lair traits rather than stated out beings to contend with), but it does mean you can add some &quot;minibosses&quot; for Heroes/etc. to have to contend with as they explore your Lair before they run int you. There's also some Lair Merits that make it much easier for non-Beast allies to help you defend your Lair (such as making your Lair have amenities like &quot;real&quot; food and water so you can have living allies in there for long periods of time, and an Internet connection to both talk to them while you're outside your Lair and so they don't get bored).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of using merits. Maybe the Dungeon linking could be a merit where the Dark Masters have the option to make their dungeons right next to each other or to use a portal or some other long-ranged transport with benefits to both methods? I'll look at Beast to see if there are ideas for that, but I hope that the basic premise of a merit for that is sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T10:45:16-07:00","id":1513880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513869#post1513869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Beasts seem to be under the impression that they're the good guys, or at least that their actions are excusable because they teach lessons. The Dark Masters know full well that they're evil and most of what they do is exclusively for their own benefit. Though, it is possible for a Dark Master to be good, just incredibly difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Lesson culture is, for many beasts, just a thing some of them use to make what they do more palatable&quot; is textual from the Beast corebook. So is &quot;Beasts are not 'good guys' and the lessons are optional.&quot; The ones that acknowledge they are not doing a good thing do not lean on explicit &quot;I am evil&quot; branding as a group (and here I note the contradiction in trying to describe other splats as knowingly evil while simultaneously leaning on the relativistic saw of &quot;the gods made Dark Masters evil according to their own definitions of evil, some of which do not align with human sensibilities&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Dark Masters do not create heroes or harm people with their mere existence. Instead, they have a very strong urge and incentive to act evil with it even making them more powerful. </div> </div> </div>Beasts do not create Heroes and their mere existence simply causes a random person within a couple of miles to lose Willpower (or, at worst, cause them to lose most of their Willpower and the ability to regain Willpower through their Anchors for maybe a week), and if this process goes badly enough for long enough the Beast will reach a level of hunger that threatens their life until they manage to feed their Hunger in a major way for dramatically reduced returns, and the main way this happens is if they don't perform less intense acts more often and/or show up for other monsters' feeding and hunting activities.<br /> <br /> For comparison, vampires directly harm people to keep active (animals are dramatically less effective at best), mummies inflict nightmarish visions on people with physical contact and power usage (and the primary insulation from this is to join a cult), and Prometheans literally blight the land around them by their continued presence (in addition to twisting up the people around them through meaningful communication and spending long enough in one of the aforementioned blights).<br /> <br /> It has never been a fair statement that the Begotten are intrinsically harmful in some worse way than the protagonists of at least a third of the other official gamelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. The gods are the enemies of the Dark Masters, and I'll probably rewrite it so that the Dark Masters are gathering in groups because they know the gods are coming for them. As for the Beasts, the True Fae respect and fear them and their goddess is fully on their side. </div> </div> </div>The True Fae interacting with the Begotten on &quot;something like equal terms&quot; is not remotely the same as &quot;respecting and fearing&quot; them and the Dark Mother's being &quot;fully on their side&quot; amounts to the fact that they have access to the abilities they have and the potential for a religious experience that takes them from empty to full Willpower and a nudge in the right direction.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. The Dark Masters aren't easily set into types. For player versatility and based on feedback I got for a previous fan gameline attempt, I didn't include an X-Splat, just a Y-Splat. Each Dark Master is hand-crafted by a god and can be fairly unique.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> 9. The Dark Masters are fundamentally meant to be final bosses or commanders of dungeons. They are anything from Sephiroth to Sauron to Ainz to the Overlord from the Overlord games to the Dungeon Keeper. They are not meant to be the monsters of myth or nightmares. </div> </div> </div>And where this is getting fumbled is that &quot;final boss&quot; and &quot;dungeon commander&quot; are not consistent narrative entities in the way that &quot;vampire&quot; or &quot;artificial life&quot; or &quot;werewolf&quot; are. These are roles that all sorts of different things can fill even in the overlap between them as separate concepts, whereas you've built lore that pins them down in a moderately specific fashion.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, on the other end of things, if you're going to say that Dark Masters's dungeons are in the physical world as a source of danger, it'd probably be wise to dedicate some attention to how Dark Masters, yknow,interact with the modern world. The Arisen of Mummy: the Curse have Tombs and cults that can be everything from hidden rooms in a corporate office building to sprawling labyrinths on the border of a remote village, but if you've specified that Dark Masters' dungeons take up physical space and their minions have physical needs then it's worth examining how generating an entire real ecosystem affects the neighbors \u2014 Beasts can get away with it because the Lair is an unusually real imaginary space located in a dimensional nexus and any native fauna are sustained by playing to type, but if the Dark Orb is folding space or pushing buildings out of the way (and if the dungeon can't be relocated) then you need to address what it means for a character that their (secret?) base of operations is a treasure trove of resources that uninvited guests can refresh just by barging in (and that can be materially blocked or shunned).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T11:33:46-07:00","id":1513883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513869#post1513869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. There is no kinship. Dark Masters don't have an innate connection to the other creatures in the Chronicles of Darkness world that makes them more likely to like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the more oover hyped things about Beasts. They get a one positive shift on making a first impression for social maneuvering. So, when a Beast first meets another supernatural, they can smooth over initial hostility, or get a fairer shake to an honest good faith offer. Everything else from there has to come from longer term relationship building (or failing to do so). Beasts can easily squander that first impression. They can just outright negate it by not immediately leaning into soft leverage (even if it's just RP instead of rolling). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Beasts seem to be under the impression that they're the good guys, or at least that their actions are excusable because they teach lessons. </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't think they're good guys, they think they were forced to be the bad guys. Some are fine being the bad guys, some aren't, some try to excuse their actions, some don't. Lessons are explicitly something Beasts make up as an excuse; not something that has any real validity to it. They know they have no supernatural imperative to do this. They're preference for it, stems from Sages and Oracles (what preceded the ego-corrupted Heroes of modern nights) using their existence to teach lessons.<br /> <br /> Basically, the big difference here is that humanity shaped the Beasts into what they are, because humans wanted moral narratives with good guys and bad guys, and the Beasts got shackled to being the bad guys by humanity instead of some more distant creator deity. Humans wanted greedy dragons sitting on piles of gold so heroes could conquer both a literal monster and a figurative moral ill. Humanity lost control over the narrative, so Beasts are left to either take control of the narrative for themselves, or at least reinterpret it for their own benefit, because the creators that abandoned the purpose they shaped Beasts for are constantly right in front of them. That conflict is always immediately in their face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. I don't mind that the Lairs in Beast aren't in the physical world, but the Dark Master dungeons are in the physical world. This is, in essence, to put them in more constant danger. They have to worry about far more threats attacking them than the Beasts do. </div> </div> </div>Ultimately though, the CofD are set in the modern times. What, exactly, stops Task Force Valkyrie from just using some drones to bomb a physical dungeon into rubble before they send in troops to finish it off? One of the reasons for Beasts (and not just Beasts, lots of other supernaturals can do this too) to create bases that aren't in the physical world is so that they still matter to modern conflicts. Even hunters with &quot;mundane&quot; tech can't simply be forced to go through a &quot;dungeon&quot; like you're trying to emulate if it exists in the physical world in a meaningful way. You'll either need to create a magical reason why enemies can't skip rooms to the point where &quot;exists on Earth&quot; and &quot;exists in a pocket dimension,&quot; is mild flavor, or Dark Masters are going to have to be even more narrow in concept to be able to construct dungeons that work in a modern reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Dark Masters do not create heroes or harm people with their mere existence. Instead, they have a very strong urge and incentive to act evil with it even making them more powerful. </div> </div> </div>The same is true of Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Beasts, the True Fae respect and fear them and their goddess is fully on their side. </div> </div> </div>The Gentry have no unified opinion of Beasts. The Dark Mother doesn't have their back in any fashion that really matters. She's not swooping in to help them out of bad situations. She's not sending them dreams of warning of imminent danger. They aren't her only children, even if they're the ones she offers the most direct power to. She expects them to care for themselves. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. Dark Masters have grand ambitions as a core part of their gameplay. I've seen gamelines (I think a fan gameline, Genius the Transgression, but I don't remember for sure) where a fourth aspiration is added in. What I did was change that Aspiration into their Virtue equivelant (their Megalomania) because it's something that can never be truly satisfied. Basically, Dark Masters persue their own personal goals and such. </div> </div> </div>Beasts get Legend in the same place... Legend is more in context with the meta-narrative nature of Beast, but Beasts are driven to become monsters that are talked about for ages; whether they die or are still stalking humanity.<br /> <br /> A lot of general CofD fans are also not going to like going back to the &quot;real world mental health conditions as character traits,&quot; thing. Derangements were dropped for a good reason. More narrative terms like Legend avoid such things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. The Dark Masters aren't easily set into types. For player versatility and based on feedback I got for a previous fan gameline attempt, I didn't include an X-Splat, just a Y-Splat. Each Dark Master is hand-crafted by a god and can be fairly unique. </div> </div> </div>Each Beast, Changeling, and Deviant is fairly unique, despite having multiple splats. X-splats don't stop high levels of customization in character design. Two splats actually helps make each character unique because each combo pushes characters in different directions on top of all the mechanical options. Splats can vary wildly in scope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9. The Dark Masters are fundamentally meant to be final bosses or commanders of dungeons. They are anything from Sephiroth to Sauron to Ainz to the Overlord from the Overlord games to the Dungeon Keeper. They are not meant to be the monsters of myth or nightmares. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the CofD is a setting about monsters of myth, both ancient and modern. Roles such as &quot;final boss&quot; or &quot;commander of dungeon,&quot; are things that are drawn out of unique takes on classic concepts. Forsaken is a game about werewolves, that has a unique take on werewolves and human-spirit hybrids that are defined by their need to hunt, which expands out into the kinds of concepts the game encourages. Coming at it from the opposite direction feels like a problem. Trying to make a game about &quot;spirit hunters&quot; is going to be hard to pull off because even if you have some solid inspirations, getting the scope of what they do, how they do it, and why they do it to mesh is going to be much harder than starting from &quot;how do you take this archetypal monster, and put a distinct spin on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the idea of using merits. Maybe the Dungeon linking could be a merit where the Dark Masters have the option to make their dungeons right next to each other or to use a portal or some other long-ranged transport with benefits to both methods? I'll look at Beast to see if there are ideas for that, but I hope that the basic premise of a merit for that is sound. </div> </div> </div>Beasts just... link their Lairs if they want to, that doesn't require a Merit, esp. because it's a bit of a mixed bag to charge people for. If a Beast doesn't defend their Lair well, and is linked to the rest of their Brood, the rest of the Brood now has to contend with invaders getting into their Lairs too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T12:22:33-07:00","id":1513886,"title":"","content":"Since Satchel and Arms handled the misconceptions, I'm gonna bring it back around to the project with the second major thought I had when reading it.<br /> <br /> I think the concept as a splat is a little anemic, but one idea that might really work is to instead craft the concept as a sort of sub-template(s) that you can append to other splats, taking ques from Deviant's Forms, Imperial Mysteries' archmage template, and Contagion Chronicle's Vectors*. You can actually take a lot of your setting conceits for the Dark Masters and rework it into gameline agnostic sources of temptation and power, and even break up the overall package into particular packages to offer more &quot;Final Boss&quot; powers and tools to characters where such may not readily be apparent-Beasts, for instance, might not need dungeon mechanics, but the options for increased survivability might be appealing for them, where as a Promethean Dark Master has plenty of good reasons for wanting to connect his various Hovels and Safe Spaces together and have a &quot;quick escape&quot; clause at the ready for them. THis also makes it less work for you in terms of needing to justify a whole piece of setting and metaphysics, because this sort of idea fits the amount of &quot;space&quot; the idea of a Final Boss can occupy.<br /> <br /> *Getting specific in the explanation, the way that Forms change any Deviant that's more significant that Variations and Scars but less significant than Origin or Clade, the archmage template as a general &quot;amplifies what you're already doing&quot; sort of thing, and Vectors as being operable sets of powers that aren't reliant upon any one game's internal metaphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-04-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T14:11:22-07:00","id":1513893,"title":"","content":"Okay, looking at all your feedback so far, I think that Dark Masters might be best as a sub-template. This is especially because of the points that everyone raises that any supernatural creature could potentially fill out the final boss role. So, it would need to be a sub-template that can apply to multiple supernatural creatures. But even with the forms and archmage, I am far more familiar with main splats than sub-templates. This is especially since I'm not familiar at all with vectors. And there aren't as many sub-templates as main splats, as far as I can tell. So, I have no idea how to make a sub-template, especially a sub-template that would work with multiple supernatural types rather than just one. I'll need to think this through a lot more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T16:46:01-07:00","id":1513900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513893#post1513893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, looking at all your feedback so far, I think that Dark Masters might be best as a sub-template. This is especially because of the points that everyone raises that any supernatural creature could potentially fill out the final boss role. So, it would need to be a sub-template that can apply to multiple supernatural creatures. But even with the forms and archmage, I am far more familiar with main splats than sub-templates. This is especially since I'm not familiar at all with vectors. And there aren't as many sub-templates as main splats, as far as I can tell. So, I have no idea how to make a sub-template, especially a sub-template that would work with multiple supernatural types rather than just one. I'll need to think this through a lot more.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to use the exact model of Vectors (or Forms or the Archmage Template, for that), and in fact while it can be useful for ideas, doing it exactly like that wouldn't work because Vectors are designed to encourage cross-gameline interaction, where as you want the Final Bosses to stand more alone. It sounds like you might not have the books we mentioned (Deviant: the Renegades, Imperial Mysteries, the Contagion Chronicle, or, for that matter, Hurt Locker, since a merit template is also a viable way to go about it, and Inferno which is already a game of otherworldly entities driven to motivate evil for their own needs and offer power that can apply to multiple splats) so let me see if I can give some broad ideas on how to go about it.<br /> <br /> The two big questions to answer:<br /> <br /> 1) Do you want the subtemplate to be something you can &quot;buy in&quot; to ala Merit dots, or do you want it to be more like applied like...templates, explaining that a little bit more: do you want it to operate a bit like how archmasters or Bale Hounds, where you either start off assuming the subtemplate is in play or otherwise you can otherwise go do a narrative act to pick it up (roleplay the Threshhold Seeking in the case of archmasters, roleplay the meeting and bargaining with Soulless Wolf in the case of the Bale Hounds)?<br /> 2) Do you want to have more of the benefits of taking up a subtemplate(s) up-front and immediate upon becoming a Dark Master, or do you want it more granular and built up piece by piece? (It can be a sort-of both, but leaning one way or another will be useful for structuring)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T05:53:02-07:00","id":1513943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513900#post1513900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't have to use the exact model of Vectors (or Forms or the Archmage Template, for that), and in fact while it can be useful for ideas, doing it exactly like that wouldn't work because Vectors are designed to encourage cross-gameline interaction, where as you want the Final Bosses to stand more alone. It sounds like you might not have the books we mentioned (Deviant: the Renegades, Imperial Mysteries, the Contagion Chronicle, or, for that matter, Hurt Locker, since a merit template is also a viable way to go about it, and Inferno which is already a game of otherworldly entities driven to motivate evil for their own needs and offer power that can apply to multiple splats) so let me see if I can give some broad ideas on how to go about it.<br /> <br /> The two big questions to answer:<br /> <br /> 1) Do you want the subtemplate to be something you can &quot;buy in&quot; to ala Merit dots, or do you want it to be more like applied like...templates, explaining that a little bit more: do you want it to operate a bit like how archmasters or Bale Hounds, where you either start off assuming the subtemplate is in play or otherwise you can otherwise go do a narrative act to pick it up (roleplay the Threshhold Seeking in the case of archmasters, roleplay the meeting and bargaining with Soulless Wolf in the case of the Bale Hounds)?<br /> 2) Do you want to have more of the benefits of taking up a subtemplate(s) up-front and immediate upon becoming a Dark Master, or do you want it more granular and built up piece by piece? (It can be a sort-of both, but leaning one way or another will be useful for structuring)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have Deviant: the Renegades, Imperial Mysteries, and Hurt Locker. I have Inferno as well. But Deviant is the newest game I have so I'm not fully familiar with it yet, and I always had a bit of trouble with Mage even though I like it a lot.<br /> <br /> However, telling me about Hurt Locker and Inferno helped me a lot. I'm very familiar with both those books. So, I'm starting to get an idea of what to do right away. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Now, for the questions:<br /> 1. I think it being something that you need to do a narrative act to pick up would be best.<br /> 2. I want it to be more gradual and built up piece by piece. Doing both might work, but it would have to lean towards gradual build up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:54:42-07:00","id":1513968,"title":"","content":"Right, so this is a long one, and most of it was made before the idea of them being a sub-template was tossed around, but I personally like the idea of them as a full template better so I'm posting this anyway. Most of it was made as I thought of it, but I did try to organize it at least somewhat by topic.<br /> <br /> I would recommend against requiring too many rules from books other than the corebook unless completely necessary, such as using Hunter the Vigil 2e for the minion creation system, as it means only people with that book can use this one properly.<br /> <br /> On that note, I would also recommend a greater emphasis on minions and their use, as it would make goals such as the conquest of a city seem more viable if the minions seem important and useful, and would also be something that really helps set this game apart from the others in the Chronicles of Darkness. As such I would recommend a minion design system that is distinct from Hunter, as it would make them seem more unique to this game and a more important part of it.<br /> <br /> I like that you have different levels of minions, but I would suggest something more akin to a Tier system, with a Tier 0 acting as Minions useful for logistics work such as building or keeping track of things or moving stuff around, but which are generally useless for combat and would get beaten by a typical mortal with little effort, a Tier 1 able to generally take on most mortals in a fight, Tier 2 being more akin to other supernatural creatures, and Tier 3 being powerful even by the standards of most supernaturals. Tier 0s would be easy to get and without much of a limit, Tier 1s would be plentiful and still fairly easily made, Tier 3s would be more difficult to make but with a decent number being possible, and Tier 3s would be difficult to make and very limited (mini-bosses, essentially). Minions would have powers that could be taken representing their abilities, with different powers being locked behind certain Tiers. The lower the Tier, the more loyal they are and the harder it is for them to disobey.<br /> <br /> One idea I would recommend is for it to be possible for minions to, through sufficient effort, restore a destroyed Dark Orb, to touch on the trope of the evil overlord being resurrected by their servants after supposedly being killed by the heroes (naturally making way for a sequel in the process). As far as Dungeons would go, I would recommend both having Dungeon traits that represent things about rooms, similar to Beast, as well as Dungeon Merits, as others have suggested.<br /> <br /> You've brought up the idea that all Dark Masters are created as unique entities by the Dark Gods, however I feel like simply not having an equivalent to Clan or Auspice makes them feel incomplete rather than unique, so I would recommend either A: adding in general archetypes based on how the Gods intended them to punish humanity, or B: go all in on the unique aspect, adding in traits that alter how they work (things like being immune to an element such as heat or cold or electricity, having a mind that can't be read or controlled, having the natural ability to enter Twilight, the ability to regenerate bashing damage each turn for free, etc), almost similar to the Deathbed Transformation abilities but weaker and which apply regardless of form, the idea being that they were simply designed that way.<br /> <br /> I would personally choose option B, as it seems more interesting to me and seems like it would fit better with your original idea. If going with this idea, I would also move some of the weaker seeming Deathbed Transformation abilities to this new type of ability, such as breathing underwater, and either removing them from the Deathbed Transformation list or buffing those ones up to make them stronger (maybe instead of just breathing underwater, they gain the ability to do that and to swim fast and maneuver easily underwater, for example), as well as buffing some of the Deathbed Transformation effects in general. I would also suggest removing the ability for some Dark Masters to always be in their Deathbed Transformations in favor of using this system to represent less human ones instead, as that way the Deathbed Transformation still seems more special.<br /> <br /> How powerful do you want individual Dark Masters to be, minions aside? Like, are we talking &quot;can equal most other Templates&quot; kind of powerful or &quot;can take on a pack of Werewolves solo and stand a chance at winning&quot; kind of powerful? To be frank some of the powers seem a bit weak even for that first option and I may have some suggestions for them, but it depends on how powerful you actually want them to be. I would personally recommend going wild with it. You've said that you wanted them to be final bosses, and the Chronicles of Darkness doesn't really concern itself much with balancing splats against each other anyway (if they did then Mages wouldn't be able to eradicate someone with 5 dots in an Arcanum while also being able to make the Spell not Withstood using an exceptional success), so there isn't really much of a reason to not make them really powerful, given the idea that they are supposed to be attacked often and also do things that invite attack often.<br /> <br /> Another idea that could help with the final boss aesthetic is to have it so that at certain Dark Power ratings a Dark Master gains additional transformations, allowing for more powerful ones to have more than two &quot;stages&quot; to their battle, representing more dangerous bosses. Something that may help with the idea of making each Dark Master unique is to give Deathbed Transformations less specific powers; instead of &quot;Extra Legs&quot; which grant a bonus to speed, they can have &quot;Enhanced Speed&quot; which grants them additional Speed and then presents a number of suggested features that could provide that bonus, such as extra legs, the ability to simply run faster, a kind of dark engine that propels the Dark Master forward with a dark shadow trail left behind as they move, and so on. This could help a lot when designing unique forms.<br /> <br /> Personally I would tone down the apparent fear of Mages in the stereotype sections, as it kind of goes against the idea of their arrogance and power, and it is also generally absent for Leviathans, many of whom would likely be more terrifying and powerful than the majority of Mages because they gain power earlier by just having access to Apotheosis and the high level powers that come with it. In particular, if a Dark Master truly had a nuke that they had stolen from the government, a Mage wouldn't be any more of a threat in the face of a nuke than a Leviathan. As well, given the idea that they are supposed to be final bosses, they probably should be able to take on Mages (as well as Leviathans, for that matter) as well, in addition to being confident that they can.<br /> <br /> As far as the Gods go, I would once again recommend giving them more unique systems as opposed to using the systems from Hunter, as it would make them seem more distinct and important to the game (and could also allow for making them more powerful and threatening), and also making them less likely to get directly involved, instead sending primarily their servants. If a conflict with a God does occur, they should be extremely powerful but able to be beaten, and there should be great benefits to be had from doing so. Basically, anything that should be important to the game (Minions, Dungeons, Gods) should likely have their own systems instead of directly using ones from other gamelines, as it will make them seem more important and unique. Another good step would be fleshing out the society and culture of the Gods and making them seem less uniform and more unique. For one thing, the idea of them all getting together in a meeting and deciding that humanity should worship them for nothing would probably be better if reference was made to a council of their leaders coming to the decision, as it once again makes them seem less homogeneous. Also, an extremely minor adjustment, I would suggest replacing the reference to spirits of Rank 4 and 5 in the Gods section with spirits of Rank 6 and higher, as they are the entities more commonly described as being god-like in nature.<br /> <br /> Reading some of the other posts, I personally find the idea of them being a sub-template far less interesting, and I think it's fine to have them as a full template as long as some things are fleshed out (Minions, Deathbed Transformations, Dungeons, as well as the Gods and some of the Dark Master abilities and powers.) Overall, I am quite interested in this. I don't have much experience with sub-templates, so I can't help much there, but if you do decide to make them a full template I would be willing to try and help out with it, though I can't promise I'll do so especially quickly as I tend to be a bit slow on these things, but I can do my best as long as life doesn't get in the way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T13:21:02-07:00","id":1513969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1513657-cofd-fan-gameline-where-you-play-as-a-final-boss?p=1513968#post1513968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so this is a long one, and most of it was made before the idea of them being a sub-template was tossed around, but I personally like the idea of them as a full template better so I'm posting this anyway. Most of it was made as I thought of it, but I did try to organize it at least somewhat by topic.<br /> <br /> I would recommend against requiring too many rules from books other than the corebook unless completely necessary, such as using Hunter the Vigil 2e for the minion creation system, as it means only people with that book can use this one properly.<br /> <br /> On that note, I would also recommend a greater emphasis on minions and their use, as it would make goals such as the conquest of a city seem more viable if the minions seem important and useful, and would also be 